4. Other Rust crates of the PDrive programs (pdrive, pdrived, pdrive-app)
   - Vendored in the source archive pdrive-for-linux-<version>.tar.xz under vendor/, each
     with its own licence files.
   - THIRD_PARTY_CRATES.txt in that archive lists name, version and licence expression of
     each crate, generated from `cargo metadata`.
   - To list the dependencies of a source checkout with their licences, run for example
     `cargo license` (cargo-license) or `cargo about generate` (cargo-about, which also
     collects the licence texts). The list changes with Cargo.lock: it is not reproduced here.

   NuGet packages (inside the NativeAOT library, see item 1): after
   scripts/build-native.sh, `dotnet list package --include-transitive` run on
   third_party/sdk gives the packages and versions; their licences are in the .nuspec or
   LICENSE files of each package (tools such as nuget-license can summarise them).

5. System libraries
